After having several discussion on this offline, the tl;dr is that the easiest solution, _for now_ at least is to change the FoldRule to not consider nullable for IsNull/IsNotNull as the semantics have changed significantly in ESQL.
Essentially remove this section:
```
            if (e instanceof IsNotNull isnn) {
                if (isnn.field().nullable() == Nullability.FALSE) {
                    return new Literal(e.source(), Boolean.TRUE, DataTypes.BOOLEAN);
                }
            } else if (e instanceof IsNull isn) {
                if (isn.field().nullable() == Nullability.FALSE) {
                    return new Literal(e.source(), Boolean.FALSE, DataTypes.BOOLEAN);
                }

```
so that `FoldNull` becomes:
```
    public static class FoldNull extends OptimizerExpressionRule<Expression> {

        public FoldNull() {
            super(TransformDirection.UP);
        }

        @Override
        protected Expression rule(Expression e) {
             if (e instanceof In in) {
                if (Expressions.isNull(in.value())) {
                    return Literal.of(in, null);
                }
            } else if (e instanceof Alias == false
                && e.nullable() == Nullability.TRUE
                && Expressions.anyMatch(e.children(), Expressions::isNull)) {
                    return Literal.of(e, null);
                }
            return e;
        }
    }
```

Remains to be seen if the tests pass but this change should be small enough that if compatible, should be backported to 8.13 as well.

